    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0771" n="721" xml:id="pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 181.921/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Bandholtz to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-13">13 November, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Hungarian prisoners of war in Siberia.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>People are coming almost daily to the office of the American Mission,
                        making heart-rending appeals for the liberation of their sons, husbands and
                        relatives now held as prisoners of war at Vladivostok, and elsewhere in
                        Siberia or Japan.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>If there is any information available relative to the probable date of
                        liberation of these prisoners, or any other information concerning their
                        disposition, it is requested that same be furnished this Mission.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. H. Bandholtz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
